## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to model non-rigid objects and integrate deformation estimation with robotic manipulation under strict latency constraints. It also probes on-device few-shot adaptation and data strategy across synthetic and real data.

## Key Concepts
- Non-rigid pose + deformation
- Photometric, silhouette, and temporal losses
- Differentiable cloth priors for realism
- Edge-optimized, multi-branch architecture
- Lightweight 5-shot on-device adaptation

## Code Example
```javascript
function forward(inputRGB) {
  const features = encoder(inputRGB);
  const pose = poseBranch(features);
  const deform = deformBranch(features);
  return { pose6DoF: pose, deformationField: deform };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to evaluate generalization to unseen fabrics and lighting
- How to robustly handle occlusions and fast motion in clutter

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes on-device real-time hazard detection and 3D distance estimation under unseen categories, reflecting safety-critical constraints common in field deployments.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time monocular depth on edge
- On-device meta-learning (5-shot)
- Synthetic+real data with domain randomization
- Temporal tracking and occlusion robustness
- Evaluation: detection, depth error, latency

## Code Example

```javascript
function forward(img, backbone, detectorHead, depthHead) {
  const feats = backbone.extract(img);
  const boxes = detectorHead.predict(feats);
  const depth = depthHead.predict(feats);
  return { boxes, depth };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you ablate depth head accuracy vs. detector latency?
- What failure modes dominate in cluttered sites, and how would you mitigate them?

